#N canvas 20 20 3200 2800 12;
#X text 20 20 u_present -- THE SHARED HALF OF DEVICE PRESENCE. It owns the one tick every c_presence ages on \, and the ONE bounded wire.sh recovery that serves every device. It keeps no per-device state at all: a c_presence instance inside each m_ layer decides whether ITS device is lost \, and this file only counts how many are., f 84;
#X text 20 190 creation arg 1: the SETTLE delay in ms before the tick starts. creation arg 2: the TICK interval in ms. creation arg 3: the GIVE-UP count \, in ticks after the first loss. inlets: none. outlets: none. It talks on presence and err \, and forks wire.sh through [shell]., f 84;
#X declare -path ../mac-stubs;
#X text 20 330 ⛔ THE SETTLE IS COUPLED TO u_init's LAST STAGE \, exactly the way u_tempo's 4000 is \, and for the same reason -- ref/module/boot.md holds the stage table both numbers answer to. Start the tick at loadbang instead and the first re-wire lands inside init-assert.sh's window \, where that gate requires EXACTLY ONE wire.sh and would go red for a reason that has nothing to do with what it tests. CHANGE A STAGE TIMING AND THIS CHANGES WITH IT., f 84;
#X text 20 520 ⚠️ ONE SHARED RE-WIRE MEANS ONE SHARED BOUND \, and coalescing is the whole reason this file exists rather than a copy of the recovery inside each m_. Two devices unplugged together must not double the fork rate: the counter runs while ANY source is lost and resets when NONE is \, so the rig gets eight attempts whether one cable or three came out., f 84;
#X text 20 700 ⚠️ IT FORKS Pd \, AND THE BOUND IS WHY THAT IS ALLOWED AT ALL. Phase 4's rule is one fork per load and NEVER per event -- written against error logging \, which cascades without limit. This cannot cascade: the counter ticks once per interval while something is missing \, mod 4 forks on every fourth tick \, and moses stops it dead at the give-up. ⚠️ THE FIRST VERSION OF THIS GAVE UP AFTER 12 SECONDS AND IT WAS USELESS -- nobody reseats a cable that fast \, and the very first hardware test missed the window entirely. wire.sh costs 133 ms \, is idempotent \, and ten forks back to back produced no audio complaint. All measured before the rule was bent., f 84;
#X text 20 930 THE QUIETER BUG THE SHARED RE-WIRE ALSO FIXES. wire.sh's three aconnect -d lines undo mother's own autoconnect \, but that undo has ALREADY RUN by the time a device enumerates late -- so a device plugged in after boot can land on the Launchpad's channel block \, which is the phantom-control incident wire.sh's own comments record. Nothing noticed it before. Re-running wire.sh fixes it \, and that is an argument for one shared owner rather than a recovery per device., f 84;
#X text 20 1140 ⛔ THE TICK GOES OUT BEFORE THE RECOVERY STEP RUNS \, off the trigger below \, and the order is the design. Pd is synchronous and depth-first \, so every c_presence has aged and any lost message has already been counted by the time the recovery reads the gate. Reverse it and every loss is acted on one whole interval late., f 84;
#X text 20 1330 THE ROSTER PRINT IS A LIVENESS SIGNAL AND NOTHING ELSE. It says how many layers registered \, once \, at settle -- so the by-hand SSH console can tell "nothing is lost" from "nothing ever registered" \, which look identical from the error bus. ⚠️ The delay is also C-9: tools/deploy.sh gates on OUTPUT and quits at about 735 ms., f 84;
